From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ricardo Pardini <ricardo@pardini.net>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 01:15:41 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] usb: gadget: u_serial: fix NULL dereference in gs_close()
 after failed open

When the port has been freed (gserial_free_line(), eg. the ACM function
was removed from a configfs gadget), gs_open() returns -ENODEV without
setting tty->driver_data. The tty core still calls ->close() for the
failed open, and gs_close() then takes port->port_lock through a NULL
port:

  Unable to handle kernel NULL pointer dereference at virtual address 0000000000000168
  pc : _raw_spin_lock_irq+0x40/0x80
  lr : gs_close+0x34/0x2d8
  Call trace:
   _raw_spin_lock_irq+0x40/0x80 (P)
   tty_release+0xf8/0x5b0
   tty_open+0x144/0x6c8
   chrdev_open+0x9c/0x1f8

Seen at shutdown when systemd reopens /dev/ttyGS0 right after the
gadget was torn down; PID 1 dies and the reboot hangs.

Return early from gs_close() when no port was attached.
---
 drivers/usb/gadget/function/u_serial.c | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/usb/gadget/function/u_serial.c b/drivers/usb/gadget/function/u_serial.c
index cdd1dfc666c4..5a81c2fec342 100644
--- a/drivers/usb/gadget/function/u_serial.c
+++ b/drivers/usb/gadget/function/u_serial.c
@@ -695,6 +695,10 @@ static void gs_close(struct tty_struct *tty, struct file *file)
 	struct gs_port *port = tty->driver_data;
 	struct gserial	*gser;
 
+	/* gs_open() failed (eg. the port was freed) before attaching a port */
+	if (!port)
+		return;
+
 	spin_lock_irq(&port->port_lock);
 
 	if (port->port.count != 1) {
-- 
2.47.3

